  "name": "catgrad",
  "description": "A categorical deep learning compiler that represents neural network architectures as open hypergraphs within the framework of symmetric monoidal categories. It provides a structured intermediate representation where tensor operations are treated as morphisms, enabling rigorous composition and optimization of complex model topologies. The system features a native CPU backend with optimized linear algebra kernels and demonstrates practical utility through implementations of modern transformer-based models like Llama, Gemma, and BERT.",
